{"title":"Career Roadmap · Emergency Planner (Junior)","role":"Emergency Planner (Junior)","summary":"An Emergency Planner (Junior) supports organizations and communities in preparing for, responding to, and recovering from emergencies and disasters. The work can include risk assessment, emergency plans, hazard mapping, evacuation planning, drills, resource planning, incident documentation, and coordination with emergency-response agencies.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc in Disaster Management is directly relevant. The strongest profile combines disaster-risk science, GIS, emergency planning, incident management, communication, data analysis, and field experience."},{"type":"p","text":"At junior level, the professional generally works under senior emergency managers, disaster-management officers, consultants, or government authorities."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Typical Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc"},{"text":"Disaster science + GIS + emergency planning"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Entry Level"},{"text":"Emergency Planner (Junior) / Disaster Management Assistant"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Experienced"},{"text":"Emergency Planner / Disaster Risk Analyst / Preparedness Specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Emergency Management Manager / Disaster Risk Reduction Lead"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Focus","Skills to Build","Proof of Progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Disaster fundamentals"},{"text":"Hazards, vulnerability, risk, environment"},{"text":"Local hazard assessment"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Risk assessment"},{"text":"GIS, hazard mapping, emergency systems"},{"text":"GIS risk map"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Emergency planning"},{"text":"Incident management, evacuation, business continuity"},{"text":"Emergency plan"}],[{"text":"Year 4 (Honours)"},{"text":"Advanced DRR"},{"text":"Disaster modelling, resilience, policy"},{"text":"Disaster-management dissertation"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Build the Disaster Science Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hazard"},{"text":"Exposure"},{"text":"Vulnerability"},{"text":"Capacity"},{"text":"Risk"},{"text":"Resilience"},{"text":"Disaster preparedness"},{"text":"Disaster response"},{"text":"Disaster recovery"},{"text":"Disaster mitigation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A useful conceptual relationship is:"},{"type":"h","text":"Disaster Risk ≈ Hazard × Exposure × Vulnerability"},{"type":"p","text":"while preparedness and response capacity can reduce potential impacts."},{"type":"h","text":"Types of hazards"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Natural"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Floods"},{"text":"Cyclones"},{"text":"Earthquakes"},{"text":"Landslides"},{"text":"Droughts"},{"text":"Heatwaves"},{"text":"Tsunamis"},{"text":"Wildfires"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human-induced/technological"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial accidents"},{"text":"Chemical incidents"},{"text":"Fires"},{"text":"Infrastructure failures"},{"text":"Transport accidents"},{"text":"Hazardous-material incidents"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Emergency Management Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the disaster-management cycle:"},{"type":"h","text":"Prevention/Mitigation"},{"type":"h","text":"Preparedness"},{"type":"h","text":"Response"},{"type":"h","text":"Recovery"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk Reduction"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the responsibilities of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government agencies"},{"text":"Emergency services"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Police"},{"text":"Fire services"},{"text":"Local authorities"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Critical infrastructure operators"},{"text":"Community organizations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Risk Assessment & GIS"},{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most valuable technical areas for an Emergency Planner."},{"type":"h","text":"GIS"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"ArcGIS fundamentals"},{"text":"GPS"},{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Spatial analysis"},{"text":"Buffer analysis"},{"text":"Overlay analysis"},{"text":"Hazard mapping"},{"text":"Population mapping"},{"text":"Infrastructure mapping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Risk mapping"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to map:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Flood-prone areas"},{"text":"Earthquake risk"},{"text":"Cyclone exposure"},{"text":"Landslide susceptibility"},{"text":"Wildfire risk"},{"text":"Critical infrastructure"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"Evacuation routes"},{"text":"Emergency shelters"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Community Disaster Risk Assessment\""},{"type":"p","text":"Map:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Major hazards"},{"text":"Population exposure"},{"text":"Vulnerable communities"},{"text":"Critical infrastructure"},{"text":"Emergency facilities"},{"text":"Evacuation routes"},{"text":"Safe zones"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Data & Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Data visualization"},{"text":"Basic Python"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Remote sensing fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Population data"},{"text":"Weather data"},{"text":"Historical disaster records"},{"text":"Infrastructure data"},{"text":"Evacuation data"},{"text":"Emergency response times"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Emergency Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Now transition from identifying risks to planning how organizations should respond."},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency plans"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Emergency Response Plans"},{"text":"Disaster Management Plans"},{"text":"Evacuation Plans"},{"text":"Business Continuity Plans"},{"text":"Crisis Communication Plans"},{"text":"Shelter Plans"},{"text":"Recovery Plans"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency planning workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Scenario development"},{"type":"h","text":"Response objectives"},{"type":"h","text":"Roles & responsibilities"},{"type":"h","text":"Resource allocation"},{"type":"h","text":"Communication procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Evacuation/shelter planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Drills & exercises"},{"type":"h","text":"Plan evaluation"},{"type":"h","text":"Incident Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the fundamentals of structured incident management:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Incident command"},{"text":"Operations"},{"text":"Planning"},{"text":"Logistics"},{"text":"Finance/administration"},{"text":"Situation reporting"},{"text":"Resource tracking"},{"text":"Communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with Incident Command System (ICS) concepts where relevant."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Business Continuity"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how organizations prepare for disruption."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Business Impact Analysis"},{"text":"Critical functions"},{"text":"Recovery priorities"},{"text":"Recovery time objectives"},{"text":"Recovery point objectives"},{"text":"Backup systems"},{"text":"Alternate facilities"},{"text":"Emergency communication"},{"text":"Crisis management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful sectors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Airports"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"IT companies"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Banks"},{"text":"Government"},{"text":"Utilities"},{"text":"Transportation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Advanced Disaster Risk Reduction"},{"type":"p","tex